  "body": "Different applications need to receive time input in different resolutions, not only \"just date\" or \"just the time part\".\r\n\r\nAs the standard already defines \"month\" and \"week\" as valid resolution points for receiving time input, and as a lot of applications need a \"year\" input (time specification with a resolution of a year) - and are currently using horribly long and hard to navigate select lists, it makes sense to offer a \"year\" input type and allow browsers to implement useful UIs to select a year easily (for example, a box showing the two decades as a 4x5 greed, similar to how the current Chrome date picker UI shows months when clicking the month selector).",
